A field beneath a struct whose values the new version narrows, which the
lens does not map: the copy that would carry the old value is the field's,
not the struct's, so the diagnostic names the field.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size:  "s" | "m" | "l"
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size:  "s" | "m"
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		id: v0_0.id
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	id: string
	meta: {
		owner: string
		size:  "s" | "m"
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0358]: the ForwardLens of v1.0 would copy v0_0.meta.size into meta.size, which does not accept every value of it
 --> history/1.0.thema:9:1
  |
9 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: both v0.0 and v1.0 declare meta.size, so a lens that does not map it copies it
  = note: meta.size in v1.0 is now "s" | "m", which has no alternative for the prior "l"
  = help: map meta.size in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
